What is GitOps?

GitOps is a deployment methodology where Git is the single source of truth for your Kubernetes cluster.

Instead of an engineer manually running commands like:

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

a GitOps tool continuously monitors your Git repository and automatically makes the Kubernetes cluster match whatever is stored in Git.

Think of Git as the desired state.

Example:

Git Repository

replicas: 5
image: payment:v2

Cluster

replicas: 3
image: payment:v1

The GitOps tool notices the difference and automatically updates the cluster until it becomes:

replicas: 5
image: payment:v2

No engineer has to SSH into servers or run kubectl manually.

Popular GitOps Tools

The two major GitOps tools are:
	•	Argo CD (Most popular in Kubernetes)
	•	Flux CD

Nowadays most organizations prefer Argo CD.

